                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b, b_1, b_2:B
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#symmetric_monoidal_category_structure Symmetric monoidal category structure
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Equipped with the tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitTensorProduct"}
              and the exchange map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}: A\otimes B \to B \otimes A
              generated by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}(a, b) = (b, a)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              becomes a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+object"} unit object
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \otimes)
              is the additive group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is the unit object, consider for any abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes \mathbb{Z} \to A
            %p
              which sends for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N} \subset \mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %mi a
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a, n) \mapsto n \cdot a \coloneqq \underbrace{a + a + \cdots + a}_{n\;summands}
                    \\,.
            %p Due to the quotient relation defining the tensor product, the element on the left is also equal to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a, n) = (a, \underbrace{1 + 1 \cdots + 1}_{n\; summands})
                    \=
                    \\underbrace{ (a,1) + (a,1) + \cdots + (a,1) }_{n\; summands}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes \mathbb{Z} \to A
              is in fact an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              Showing that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}
              is natural in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
              is trivial, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is a braiding.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma^2
              is identity, so it gives Ab a symmetric monoidal structure.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The tensor product of abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity"} distributes
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of abelian groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes \oplus_{s \in S} B_s
                    \\simeq
                    \\oplus_{s \in S} ( A \otimes B_s )
                    \\,.
          %h3#monoids Monoids
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \otimes)
              is equivalently a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \cdot)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \otimes)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdot : A \otimes A \to A
            %p
              is bilinear means by the above that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1, a_2, b \in A
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a_1 +  a_2) \cdot b = a_1 \cdot b  + a_2 \cdot b
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b \cdot (a_1 +  a_2) = b \cdot a_1 + b \cdot a_2
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+law"} distributivity law
              of the ring.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            positive we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_n
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order"} order
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in \mathbb{N}
              and positive, we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi b
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}_a \otimes \mathbb{Z}_b \simeq \mathbb{Z}_{(a,b)}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,-)
              denotes the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/greatest+common+divisor"} greatest common divisor
          %p
            A proof is spelled out for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Conrad"}> Conrad, theorem 4.1
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+commutative+monoids"} tensor product of commutative monoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+algebras+over+a+commutative+monad"} tensor product of algebras over a commutative monad
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original definition is due to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hassler+Whitney"} Hassler Whitney
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hassler+Whitney"}> Hassler Whitney
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tensor products of Abelian groups
              %strong 4
              3 (1938) 495-528
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1215/S0012-7094-38-00442-9"}> doi:10.1215/S0012-7094-38-00442-9
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p An exposition (in the case of vector spaces) is in
          %ul
            %li
              Tim Gowers,
              = succeed "," do
                %em How to lose your fear of tensor products
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.dpmms.cam.ac.uk/~wtg10/tensors3.html"} web
          %p
            and, in the further generality of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
          %ul#Conrad
            %li
              Keith Conrad,
              %em Tensor products
              (
              %a{:href => "https://kconrad.math.uconn.edu/blurbs/linmultialg/tensorprod.pdf"}> pdf
              )
